==Bulgarian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|cu|bg}} {{term|чрънъ|lang=cu}}, from {{etyl|sla-pro|bg}} {{recons|čьrnъ|lang=sla-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|bg}} {{recons|krsnos|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognates include Serbo-Croatian {{term|црн|lang=sh}}/{{term|crn|lang=sh}}, Slovene {{term|črn|lang=sl}}, Slovak {{term|čierny|lang=sk}}; Norwegian and Swedish {{term|harr||grayling|lang=sv}}, Sanskrit {{term|कृष्ण|tr=kṛṣṇá|sc=Deva}}, Old Prussian {{term|kirsnan||black|lang=prg}}.

